customManagers.description:
Bump version literals in GitHub Actions workflows annotated with `# renovate: datasource=X depName=Y`. Supports trailing-comment (hint after value) and leading-comment (hint on line above value) styles. INVARIANT: inter-field separators must use `[ 	]`, never `\s` — `\s` matches `
` and causes cross-block attribution (see PR #4). The two patterns share textually identical metadata-tail and value subpatterns; JSON has no interpolation and RE2 has no subpattern references, so edits must apply character-for-character to both. INVARIANT: the leading-comment pattern must stay anchored to line start with `(?:^|
)[ 	]*`. A bare `#[ 	]*renovate:` matches a `#` ANYWHERE on a line, so a TRAILING annotation whose NEXT line carries a version literal gets re-read as a leading one and paired with that next line's value — a phantom dep. Observed 2026-09-20 in unifi-network-mcp and unifi-protect-mcp, whose `node-version:` matrix puts one annotated lane per line: extraction yielded THREE deps, the third `depName=node-lts-22 currentValue=24.21.0`. It was inert only by luck — node.json caps node-lts-22 at `allowedVersions: "<23"`, so the mis-paired 24.x satisfied nothing and produced no updates, no warning, no dashboard entry. That protection depends entirely on the lanes being written in ASCENDING order, which makes the stolen value always N+2. Reverse the two lines and the phantom becomes `node-lts-24 @ 22.23.2`, which DOES resolve: it rewrites the 22 lane's literal to 24.21.0, the matrix silently becomes 24/24, Node 22 coverage vanishes and CI stays green because both lanes pass — the same SPLIT-BRAIN failure the github-runners customManager below exists to prevent. This is a DIFFERENT leak from the `[ 	]`-not-`\s` invariant above: that one is separators between fields crossing into the next block; this one is within-pattern, where `[^
]*?` after the literal `
` walks the following line. RE2 has no lookbehind, so the anchor has to CONSUME the newline and `replaceString` gains a leading `
`; that is safe, because auto-replace is literal `indexOf`/`matchAt`/`replaceAt` over `replaceString`, not a rerun of the regex — proven end-to-end against renovate 44.104.1's `doAutoReplace`, which rewrote only the value line and passed its own post-replace `confirmIfDepUpdated` re-extraction. The anchor is a PREFIX-only edit: the metadata-tail and value subpatterns stay character-for-character identical to the trailing-comment pattern's, so the character-for-character invariant above survives untouched. NOTE — as of 2026-09-20 no repo extending this preset writes the leading-comment style at all (the fleet's only one is compose-workflow, which extends `customManagers:githubActionsVersions` and NOT this preset), so nothing in the fleet exercises this pattern's happy path and a regression to it would be silent. Verify any edit here with a real extract run, never by eye. Reaches places the github-actions manager can't natively (matrix arrays, run-step args, env defaults).
